      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those feelings of being a mistake are a devastating weight, but they are rooted in intense pain, not in reality. Your life is not a deficit against their memory; rather, it is a continuation of your own existence. You don't have to \"move on\" in a neat way, but you can allow yourself to feel the depth of this grief without judging yourself for it. A therapist can help you untangle this complex belief that your survival is somehow an act of theft.",
